WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.780
Welcome to Grade 7 English, Unit 3:
Clothing, Fashion, and Sustainability.

2
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:13.020
This unit explores the world of clothing, fashion,
and sustainability.You will learn how clothes are made,

3
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.540
why the choices we make as consumers matter,

4
00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:22.700
and what young people around the world are doing to protect
the environment through sustainable fashion.You will build

5
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.640
your skills with multi-word verbs such as put on,

6
00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:32.520
dress up and throw away, and you will learn how the
passive voice and modal verbs describe processes,

7
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:39.960
rules and recommendations.Alongside the topic
work, you will read the story A Voice in the Valley,

8
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:48.140
about a quiet girl named Sana in highland Ethiopia who
discovers that her writing can inspire an entire community.

9
00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:54.680
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:55.350 --> 00:01:02.300
By the end of this unit, you will be able to use
vocabulary related to clothing, materials, fast fashion,

11
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:03.620
and the environment.

12
00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:11.880
You will also understand and use multi-word verbs (phrasal
verbs) such as put on, take off, dress up, throw away,

13
00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:12.560
and give away.

14
00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:20.420
You will also form sentences in the present passive ("Cotton
is grown in many countries") and past passive ("The dress

15
00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:21.560
was made by hand").

16
00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.140
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

17
00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:33.100
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: assumption,
complexity, composition, consistency, organic, toxin.

18
00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:39.080
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

19
00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.520
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

20
00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:51.280
The reading sequence includes The True Cost of Fast Fashion
and From Curtains to Catwalk: An Interview with Amara.

21
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.200
Read actively.

22
00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.940
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

23
00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:02.940
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

24
00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:06.500
The first language focus is Multi-Word Verbs.

25
00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:14.060
Multi-word verbs, often called phrasal verbs, join a
main verb to a particle such as on, off, up or away,

26
00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:21.380
and together they create a meaning the verb alone does not
carry, so put on means to wear while put off means to delay.

27
00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:28.540
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

28
00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:35.000
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1:
Describe Your Outfit with Multi-Word Verbs.

29
00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:40.100
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

30
00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:44.460
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

31
00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:48.120
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

32
00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:49.900
You are ready to begin.

33
00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:56.780
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

34
00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.740
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

35
00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:07.600
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
